From: LilSmokeOS developers
Subject: [PATCH] linux-input: reject a libc-dependent evdev wire layout

The kernel event stream uses two native-long timestamp fields, even when
32-bit musl has 64-bit time_t. The time64 header accessors are not sufficient
if stale headers expose a 24-byte event on a 32-bit target. Reject that ABI
instead of silently misinterpreting keys. Buildroot's current musl headers
provide the correct 16-byte structure.

--- a/inputdrivers/linux_input/linux_input.c
+++ b/inputdrivers/linux_input/linux_input.c
@@ -43,3 +43,7 @@
 #include <linux/input.h>
 
+typedef char linux_input_event_wire_abi_check[
+     sizeof(struct input_event) == 2 * sizeof(long) + 8 &&
+     __builtin_offsetof(struct input_event, type) == 2 * sizeof(long) ? 1 : -1];
+
 #ifndef input_event_sec
